@startuml architecture_overview
left to right direction
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

' --- breathing room (higher = less label/box overlap) ---
skinparam nodesep 72
skinparam ranksep 88
skinparam padding 8
skinparam componentPadding 12
skinparam packagePadding 10
skinparam ArrowMessageAlignment center

' --- soft palette ---
skinparam backgroundColor #F7F9FC
skinparam defaultFontColor #334155
skinparam ArrowColor #64748B
skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor #E8EDF5
  BorderColor #A8B8D0
  FontColor #334155
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #8B9CB8
  FontColor #1E293B
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FDF8EE
  BorderColor #D4C4A8
  FontColor #57534E
}

title System architecture — overview

legend
|= Arrow |= Meaning |
| --> | runtime interaction |
| ..> | dependency / config |
endlegend

together {
  package "Python process" as PY #E3F0FC {
    [Python AI system] as AI
    [WebSocket bridge] as BR
    ' Split loop: avoids one long label sitting on the bidirectional line
    BR --> AI : observations
    AI --> BR : actions
  }
}

package "Minecraft" as MC #E8F6EC {
  together {
    [Game client\n(Forge mod)] as CL
    [Game server\n(dedicated / integrated)] as SV
    CL -[hidden]down- SV
  }
}

package "BotNet" as BN #FFF4E5 {
  [Gameplay packets\n(actions, bot state, config)] as PK
}

' Short link text; full names in note (reduces crossing with sibling arrows)
BR --> CL : PLAYER
BR --> SV : SERVER_BOT

CL <--> PK
SV <--> PK

note bottom of PY
  **WebSocket** to Minecraft (one socket per mode).
  **PLAYER** — client role, local player.
  **SERVER_BOT** — server role, fake bot.
end note

@enduml
